WEBVTT

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:09.780
Hime-chan?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.980
Yes?

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.720
I bought some dorayaki from Umezono.
Let's have them with some with tea—

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.730
What are you up to?

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.260
I was cleaning up and I found 
these old New Years' cards.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.740
It just reminded me of the past.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.700
You don't say.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.710
Oh, I'm surprised this 
one ever made it here.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.510
Hime-chan

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.060
Right?

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.240
It's from Nao-chan.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.360
Oh, my...

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.270
And she didn't even write 
"Happy New Year" on the card.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.010
Huh? What is this?

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.520
Thank you for yesterday. 
-Naruse Family, Naoko

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.520
It says, "Thank you for yesterday."

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:47.930
What is this?

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.230
I can't remember.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.030
I guess I'll ask her about it
 tomorrow, in school.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.420
Who could that be?

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.410
I'll get it.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.560
Coming!

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.280
Huh?

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:06.290
Nao-chan? What's going on?

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.590
Humble apologies for this 
sudden intrusion,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.960
but could I please spend the night?

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.240
I got into a fight with my mother,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.470
so I stormed out and left a note 
saying I'd stay at Hime-chan's...

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.300
Why don't you come in first?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.730
You came at the right time.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:58.900
<b>My Paradise</b>

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:59.420
Oh, the New Year's card 
I gave you in second grade?

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.390
You were back home during that time,

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:03.670
so I came over and put it 
in the mailbox myself.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.780
So what does this "Thank 
you for yesterday'"mean?

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.040
Oh, that.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.580
Thank you so much for that!

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.020
So you remember?

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.550
I'll remember it until the day I die.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.980
What is it? What did I do for you?

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.390
Well, that...

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.460
Uh-huh?

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.780
...is a secret.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.360
Stop teasing me!

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:28.080
But explaining it would be so embarrassing.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.680
Come on. Don't say that. Please?

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.700
I'm letting you stay the night.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.810
Fine, then. Find me a Chinese bell flower

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:39.220
around Kokei Park, and I'll tell you.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.660
Really?

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.850
You can sometimes find them
growing along this street.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.350
A Chinese bell flower, huh? Got it!

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.220
It's chilly.

00:03:50.760 --> 00:03:53.200
I'm not finding any, Nao-chan!

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.200
I don't think there will be any.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.750
Good! It's better for me 
if you don't find one.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:03:59.980
I'll find one!

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.350
Now I'm committed!

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:06.340
So these flowers are purple or 
white star-shaped flowers, right?

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:07.820
That's it.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.760
Bell flower... Bell flower...

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.270
Now that I think about it,

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.930
those flowers are only around until 
September. I'll never find one!

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.590
Don't worry! You can still find one.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:21.360
In fact, you already passed 
a spot that has them.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.080
Really?

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:28.530
Gohei
Mochi

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.190
There are more further up, too,

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.530
but based on how you're currently doing,
 you won't find those, either.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:32.090
Oh, where are they?

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:33.800
Huh?

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.010
Wait, are you talking about these?

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:38.790
Aw shucks, you found it.

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:42.090
Come on! You didn't mean the real thing.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.540
You figured it out, bravo!

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.170
Then I guess I have no choice. 
I have to tell you the truth.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.560
Yay!

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.290
Incidentally, they have these 
in colored versions too.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.670
And a bunch of different ones, too

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.580
Fire Hydrant

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.580
Water Supply
Air Valve

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.960
You should try to find 
them if you're bored.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.560
Okay.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:12.370
Since I was in kindergarten, a lot 
of people said I was a weird kid.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.850
Oh, I see.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:16.410
My dad was always buying 
Showa mangas and animes,

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:21.120
CDs, LDs, VHDs, DVDs, and Blu-Rays.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.420
I didn't get a lot of that, but okay.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:26.410
Then he was always buying these soft vinyl 
monster toys of all shapes and sizes.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.980
My mom finally stopped him 
when he tried to buy a

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.760
one-meter-long space ship.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.430
Since I was also into that 
stuff in kindergarten,

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.320
I didn't really have anything 
to talk about with the other kids.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.320
I can see that.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.820
And there I was, a second-grader 
all alone on New Years Eve,

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:49.010
when you came and talked to me.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.660
Is that what happened?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.820
It is!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.580
And you've been my angel ever since.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.410
Huh? So, what did I say?

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.710
The wind is really cold!

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.420
You didn't say anything 
particularly unusual.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.440
You looked at the pottery piece I made 
during the hands-on pottery class

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.360
in the fall of second grade and you said,

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.640
"Wow, what is this? This is really cool!"

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:21.900
Oh!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:23.390
Do you remember?

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:27.400
Wait, was it that cup with the 
spiral cut out on the side?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.790
That's it!

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.690
I'm so happy you remembered!

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:38.870
I was about to throw it out 
since we were cleaning the house.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.400
But why?

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:44.080
First, I wanted to make 
a coffee cup for my mom.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.550
She really likes coffee.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.930
I'm going to make a kitty!

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.440
What about you?

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:54.870
I was thinking I'd make a...

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:59.600
I'd made it too big, and I was 
wondering what to do with it.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:07.130
Then I remember this yarn bowl I'd seen in 
one of my mother's handicraft magazines.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.050
What's a yarn bowl?

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:14.850
A container where you can put a 
yarn ball in and feed the yarn

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.590
through the cutout so the 
ball doesn't roll all over.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:21.180
So that's what that was!

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.920
Once it was fired though, everybody 
started saying stuff...

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.540
You can't drink from that!

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.210
That's no good.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.510
Why'd you make it like that?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.180
That's so useless.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:39.290
I should've just told them that 
it was a bowl for holding yarn,

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:40.960
but I didn't really have the courage.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:45.440
And hearing all that made 
me think it was useless, too.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:50.170
I took it home,
 but I didn't show it to anyone...

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:54.110
Then on our house-cleaning day I snuck out,

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.950
trying to secretly hide it in the trash...

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.360
What's that?

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.730
That's so cool!

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:14.630
Hime-chan...

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:16.400
And that color is really cute.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.820
This curly part here reminds 
me of a cat's tail.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.680
Did you make this?

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:24.590
Yeah.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.730
Wow, you're really good!

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.690
I don't know...

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.360
You really are!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:37.940
You were the only one who didn't reject 
what I made, and even praised it.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.190
I see.

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.190
That's right.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:48.180
That's so pretty!

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.080
It is.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:52.510
Hime-chan, you know?

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:53.450
Huh?

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.830
You're like Mino ware.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.350
Sorry, but I don't really get that analogy.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:03.540
There's this open-mindedness to Mino ware

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:07.460
that accepts you,
 no matter who you are.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.140
Really?

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.100
Really.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:11.910
I see.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:13.150
Exactly.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.310
It's a slumber party!

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:19.490
Should I turn off the light?

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.700
It's up to you.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.540
So let's hear it.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:27.010
Let's hear your romantic secrets.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:29.130
There are none of those.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.900
Why, do you have some?

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.620
Not right now.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.380
I figured.

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:37.270
Hey, what is that supposed to mean?

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.090
Looks like you get the tickle punishment!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:44.150
I give up! I give up! I give up!

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.980
Was it in kindergarten that we first met?

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:57.540
It must have been one of the times when 
I came back here for Obon or New Years.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.650
I mean, we knew each other by sight 
since we lived next to each other,

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:04.570
but since I was so shy, I was 
probably hard to approach.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:09.530
I might have thought that 
you had an odd feel.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.400
But you still came and talked to me.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:18.320
I think that's because you were some 
kind of wonderland or paradise.

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.060
Huh? I've never heard that before.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.300
That must have been back in first grade.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:29.700
I'm going to go buy juice, grandma!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.270
Watch out for traffic!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.610
I will! Be back soon!

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.100
I was home for Obon,

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.610
and you came out dressed like an explorer.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:45.710
I was wondering what that was about.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.460
That might have happened...

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.620
My somewhat cringey past...

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:54.150
But I was interested, so I followed you.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.010
Quietly.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:56.120
Really?

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:24.850
And then, you into the yard 
of an abandoned house.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.400
The kind of thing good boys and girls 
aren't supposed to do.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:34.120
You attached ears and eyebrows 
to a broken down car.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.970
You turned it into a cream-colored koala.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.520
I don't remember that at all.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:46.950
Probably because I was always 
doing stuff like that.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:57.790
Whatever comes out of you is always 
something I completely lack.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:59.820
I like that feeling.

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:02.160
That's... good.

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:06.600
Well, you're the only person with 
whom I can really let my guard down.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.840
Really?

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:12.410
Well, you're the only one 
who is honestly surprised

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.540
or bewildered when I do my weird stuff.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.570
So...

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.480
Yeah?

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:21.780
That yarn bowl?

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.170
Did you end up giving it to your mother?

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:24.920
Yes.

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:26.440
And was she happy?

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.460
I don't remember...

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.630
But she does still use it now and then.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.090
Really?

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.430
Then I'm glad.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:37.990
Huh?

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:42.640
That I was able to meet you, and be honest.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:49.700
I see... You're right.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:56.540
I'll prepare breakfast 

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:56.540
Sorry about today.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.840
I'll prepare breakfast 

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.840
Sorry about today. 

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.870
The bob-haired girl wanders through Tajimi

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:35.350
<b>Mini Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.980
to have yet another encounter with pottery!

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:34.410
The person she randomly meets 
has an unexpected connection to her.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.890
Next up, we have "My Mom Really Is Amazing!"

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:40.010
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:40.010
<b>My Mom Really Is Amazing!</b>

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:39.280
The power and fighting spirit are on fire!
